  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "Calculate the slope $m$ of the tangent line to the curve $f(x)=arccsc(\\sqrt{x})$ at $x=2.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of $arccsc$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccsc\\,x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[arccsc(\\sqrt{x})] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{|\\sqrt{x}|\\sqrt{{(\\sqrt{x})}^{2}-1}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}\\sqrt{x-1}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2x\\sqrt{x-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent line to the curve at $x=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={f}^{\u2032}(2) & =-\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{2-1}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
